  "id": "Compound::DB00757 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Dolasetron is shown to interact with Cyp2c9 through multiple pathways, with the core mechanism involving its binding to Cyp3a4 and subsequent participation in oxidative enzymatic activities. This binding leads to the activation of Cyp2c9, which is involved in the oxidation of various substrates, including quinones and other compounds. The evidence suggests that Dolasetron may influence Cyp2c9 through a shared pathway involving Cyp3a4, which is a well-characterized cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in drug metabolism. The presence of multiple overlapping pathways—such as the involvement of Cyp3a4 in both oxidoreductase and caffeine oxidase activities—supports a mechanism where Dolasetron modulates Cyp2c9 by targeting a common substrate or regulatory pathway. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, biologically plausible relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
